35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found out some really important things! Some rooms are way colder than others because of the sunlight, and some people use way more power. We can't just split everything equally, or some of us will freeze!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, while room differences matter, the financial volatility is the real issue. The bills fluctuate wildly, with February being over three times the cost of August. We need a system that stabilizes these payments throughout the year.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, that sounds scary! But listen, I looked into those templates and other houses, and it's a nightmare! One house spends forty minutes just reading meters. We can't have a system that takes that much work every month!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, forty minutes is a small price to pay for accuracy. My data shows some rooms use four times more power than others. Ignoring that isn't ""easy,"" it's just unfair to those paying for someone else's heater.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, accuracy is important, but the payment log shows that disputes over amounts are already causing delays and tension. If we make the system too complex, we risk further damaging our relationships over a few yen.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I get that it's unfair, but if we're too strict, people will just suffer in silence! I don't want anyone wearing a coat inside just because they're scared of the bill. We need a way to be fair without being scary!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, comfort is necessary, but we can't ignore the cost. Installing sub-meters would cost 34,000 yen per room. That's a huge upfront expense that doesn't solve the problem of the massive seasonal spikes in our bills.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, that's way too expensive! And @Shunichi, if it takes forty minutes just to read meters, imagine how long it takes to argue about them! We need a system that's simple, or we'll spend all our free time doing math!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your fear of a little arithmetic is amusing, but the reality is worse. We have a four-fold difference in usage. A ""simple"" system is just a polite way of saying some of us are paying for others' luxury.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, it's not about the arithmetic, but the friction it creates. The logs show that even small discrepancies lead to weeks of tension and late payments. We need a system that minimizes these conflict points.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, exactly! If we're always arguing, the house won't feel like a home. But @Shunichi, we can't ignore the cold rooms. Maybe we can find a middle ground where we account for the room differences without making it a chore?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, a middle ground is possible, but it must be financially sustainable. We cannot afford high installation fees, nor can we handle bills that triple in winter. Any solution must prioritize stability and low overhead.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, I agree! Stability is great, but please don't make it complicated. If we have to key in every single invoice one by one like that template I saw, it'll be a total disaster! We need something we can finish in five minutes!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, five minutes of work is a fantasy if you want actual fairness. @Ryuji, stability is fine, but not if it's achieved by averaging out a four-fold difference in usage. That's just organized unfairness.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, ""organized unfairness"" is better than a house where people avoid each other for a week after a reminder. We need a system that is predictable enough that no one feels the need to question the amount every month.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, I totally agree! Let's find a way that's predictable and kind. If we can account for the cold rooms without making it a stressful math project, everyone can finally relax and feel warm!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, kindness is good, but predictability is what prevents stress. We must avoid expensive hardware and volatile monthly costs. I believe a system that averages the annual cost into fixed monthly payments is the most rational path forward.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, that sounds way better! If the price is the same every month, we don't have to do a big scary calculation every time. As long as it's a ""set it and forget it"" kind of thing, I'm all for it!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, averaging costs is just a mask for the disparity. If one person uses four times the energy, they should pay for it. I'll vote for whatever option actually addresses the usage gap, not just the calendar.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, focusing only on the gap ignores the social cost. If we prioritize absolute precision over peace, we'll just keep fighting. I'll support a system that is simple and predictable to stop the cycle of accusations and avoidance.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
