60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option B sounds fair for the cold rooms, but it's so expensive! Option C is simple, but I'm worried people will still be scared to turn on the heat. I think Option A is the best balance!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, I agree. Option B is financially reckless given the installation costs, and Option C maintains the volatile spikes that make budgeting impossible. Option A provides the predictability I seek while avoiding high upfront expenses.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, I'm with you! Option B sounds like a total nightmare to manage every month, and Option C still means we have to do math every single time the bill comes. Option A is the fastest!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your desire for speed is predictable. However, Option A and C are both just different ways of ignoring the fact that some of us are subsidizing others. Only Option B addresses the actual usage disparity.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, Option B would likely increase the friction we're already experiencing. Constant monitoring and precise billing often lead to more accusations, not fewer. I prefer Option A because it reduces the frequency of disputes and provides stability.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I know you want it to be perfect, but if we're always watching meters, we'll never stop worrying! Option A lets us just live our lives and stay warm without the stress!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, your pursuit of absolute precision ignores the practical reality of our budget. Spending over 100,000 yen on meters is an irrational use of funds when we can achieve stability through a seasonal average.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, you're being too stubborn! Even if it's ""perfect,"" it's a huge chore. I don't want to spend my weekends doing math or arguing over meters. Option A is way more fun because it's easy!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, ""fun"" is a strange metric for financial obligations. @Ryuji, the cost of meters is a one-time investment; the cost of subsidizing a roommate's desktop and heater is a permanent tax on the efficient. I stand by Option B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, a ""permanent tax"" is a small price to pay for a home where we actually speak to each other. Option B turns us into accountants, not housemates. I'm voting for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, exactly! I want us to be friends, not accountants. @Shunichi, please understand that feeling safe and warm is more important than a perfect number. I'm voting for Option A too!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, your logic is consistent, but it is not practical. The financial volatility of our bills is a systemic risk that Option B does not solve. Option A is the only rational choice for long-term stability. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, you're just making it a job! I'm not doing that. Option A is the only one that doesn't sound like a boring homework assignment every month. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, calling fairness ""homework"" is a fascinating way to avoid responsibility. Since the rest of you prefer a comfortable delusion over mathematical truth, I'll be the lone voice of reason. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, truth without empathy is just a source of conflict. I've seen how these disputes poison the air in this house. For the sake of our peace and sanity, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,It looks like we've all made our choices! I really hope this means we can all stop worrying and just enjoy being cozy together. I'm so happy we decided this! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The decision is clear. Option A is the most rational choice, as it eliminates the risk of sudden financial spikes and avoids unnecessary installation costs. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! We did it! No more scary math every month and no more boring homework. Let's just keep it simple and have more time for fun! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Since you all prefer the convenience of a shared lie over the effort of the truth, I'll stop wasting my breath. Enjoy your ""peace"" while you're paying for each other. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I hope that by choosing predictability over precision, we can finally stop treating each other with suspicion. Let's focus on being housemates again. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
